From 4ca768bbedadcc67560f9a4683fe3229946b4f22 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kevin Barnard <kevin.barnard@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 26 Jul 2026 03:37:40 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] [minixrs] Driver: test the MinixRS link line

clang/test/Driver/minixrs.c pins the driver contract that
tooling/docs/sysroot-layout.md fixes: ld.lld, --sysroot=, unconditional
-static, both minixrs -z flags, crt1.o/crti.o/crtn.o and -L out of
<sysroot>/usr/lib, per-target compiler-rt builtins, -lc, and
<sysroot>/usr/include on the include path. Also the preprocessor defines, the
driver-relative default sysroot, and the answers to flags the platform cannot
honour: -shared is an error, -pie/-no-pie/-rdynamic are dropped without a
warning, and sanitizers are rejected.

The fixture is a new self-contained Inputs/minixrs_tree rather than new
entries in Inputs/resource_dir_with_per_target_subdir, so the patch series
stays all-new-files and cheap to rebase.

Three notes on the checks themselves, all of which come down to one FileCheck
rule: a -NOT is only tested in the gaps *between* positive matches, so text a
positive pattern consumed is never scanned.

  - the no-dots assertion gets its own FileCheck run, anchored on the
    earliest token of the cc1 line and nothing else. Every path that could
    carry an unfolded "bin/../sysroot" spelling comes after "-triple", so the
    -NOT still covers all of them, while matching "-triple" consumes no path
    text of its own. It cannot instead live in the default-sysroot run: the
    -L pattern there spells the middle of the path {{[^"]*}}, which matches
    -- and so swallows -- the very spelling the -NOT must reject.
  - the happy-path negatives (-dynamic-linker, -shared, -pie) are
    --implicit-check-not rather than inline CHECK-NOT lines, which would have
    scanned only the few tokens between the second -z pair and crt1.o.
  - the claimed-flag run is anchored on ld.lld and -static before its
    negatives. A run of bare -NOTs also passes on empty output, or on a
    driver that died before emitting a link line.

Mutation-tested from both sides. Source side: deleting the remove_dots call
in MinixRS.cpp, and dropping ClaimAllArgs(OPT_pie), each fail the test. Test
side: every directive was broken in turn with a control token chosen to land
in that directive's own scan region, and each broke the test; the unmutated
file passes.

check-clang-driver: 1403 tests, 1320 passed, 82 unsupported, 1 XFAIL, 0
failures.
